{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/657216-questions-from-an-stranger-on-wolve-s-lands","id":657216,"title":"Questions from an stranger on Wolve's Lands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-08T17:54:00-07:00","id":657216,"title":"Questions from an stranger on Wolve's Lands","content":"i used to play as a Nuwisha..a Lot. and its been years since i last played werewolf.<br /> <br /> so i got a couple of questions.<br /> One: What did you had to roll in order to go to the umbra again? O.o<br /> Two: how fast can a garou regenerate damage? do they soak damage in hominid form as well?<br /> three: any examples for the Rite of Passage ?<br /> Four: mid spoiler, what was the deal with the White Howlers? i seem to recall something about them Not being able to return or chaos would happend (meaning that the black spirals are not actually them)..or was it the Croatans with the Souleater?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:18:56-07:00","id":657245,"title":"","content":"1- Gnosis<br /> 2 - one non-aggravated level per turn; being in combat might require a roll. If lupus, they regenerate in Homid, but homids don't regenerate in Homid. Agg is one level per day.<br /> 3 - That's really wide open; if not counting the old adventure book of the same name, it can be any challenge that might crop up, even something that might be incredibly difficult.<br /> 4 - They were entirely corrupted into the Black Spiral Dancers. They ceased to exist as White Howlers and became something else. The totem doesn't acknowledge the tribe as continuing to exist. The Croatan, however, are generally described as being bound to keeping the Eater of Souls away. In some scenarios of Apocalypse, however, the EoS is already coming back due to the &quot;sacrifice&quot; of the Ravnos Clan founder, so that could be fluffed as being a reason for having Turtle's tribe pop up again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T11:07:19-07:00","id":658173,"title":"","content":"Two more question<br /> How to get a totem? I know The chars have that backgrounds but i didnt understood The system<br /> Same with rituals.<br /> A garou has The Rituals background in lvl 5, he can buy a lvl 5 ritual then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T12:32:00-07:00","id":658257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/657216-questions-from-an-stranger-on-wolve-s-lands?p=658173#post658173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two more question<br /> How to get a totem? I know The chars have that backgrounds but i didnt understood The system</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're still in chargen, you just pay Background points for a Pack or Personal Totem. If you're in play, someone has to use Rite of the Totem, and then people have to pay xp for improving the Background.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same with rituals.<br /> A garou has The Rituals background in lvl 5, he can buy a lvl 5 ritual then? </div> </div> </div>You only buy rites if you're still in chargen (in play they're free but require a week per level to learn), but yes, the minimum level of Rituals Knowledge to know a rite is the rite's level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T01:33:30-07:00","id":659104,"title":"","content":"Also, it would be nice if you play up the whole quest to find the Spirit and persuade it into joining and shepharding the pack it will stay with for ages to come. There are loads of brilliant stories and roleplaying opportunities in that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T06:56:04-07:00","id":665654,"title":"","content":"I don't like totem as a background. I normally make the characters quest for a totem as the first story of a chronicle with the players giving me a list of totems they might be interested in having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T07:37:00-07:00","id":665682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/657216-questions-from-an-stranger-on-wolve-s-lands?p=665654#post665654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like totem as a background. I normally make the characters quest for a totem as the first story of a chronicle with the players giving me a list of totems they might be interested in having.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much just another part of a prelude, though. Totem is how you nail it down in mechanical terms, just like how much they have in assets, or their connection to past generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}